research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a1a2.result.json:16:  "tail": "A1/A2 is complete. No item or page was edited.\n\nArtifacts:\n\n- [Provenance ledger](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.provenance.jsonl) — 61/61 items, 26 verified source URLs.\n- [Audit findings](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.findings.md) — exact repair proposals and full coverage statement.\n- [Proof contracts](/home/lazyinspirit/Projects/prestige-math-library/research/audit/wave11-real-analysis.proof-contracts.json) — 55/55 proofs, 377 steps, 703 citations, and 440 boundary cases.\n\nMaterial findings:\n\n- `ex-integral-test-applied-to-the-p-series` falsely says no primitive can exist at \\(p=1\\). Every continuous function on an interval has an integral-function primitive; only a named logarithmic form is unavailable here. [Encyclopedia of Mathematics](https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Integral_calculus)\n- `thm-linearity-of-the-integral` step 4.2 cites nonexistent step 6.3; the correct inputs are steps 2.3, 2.4, and 3.2.\n- Six unused Fact lines produce eleven honest `citation-uses` exceptions and are queued as owner-only deletions.\n- Three standard claims remain `established-knowledge` pending Alpha concurrence.\n- The strict contract check covers 55/55 and reports exactly the 12 documented source-item defects—one missing step reference and eleven unused citations—with zero warnings.\n\nAll 61 items, 55 proofs, 790 declared relationships, and 158 distinct dependency targets were read. The report is ready for Alpha/A3."
