research/audit/wave11-refuter-tasks/thm-ftc-first-part.md-2760-[L7] Ordered-field arithmetic: multiplying an inequality by a nonnegative quantity preserves it, a positive real has a positive inverse, and the order is total and transitive ([[def-ordered-field]], [[def-complete-ordered-field]]).
