research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations.prompt.md-137-[L1] If $u$ is integrable on $[a,b]$ with values in $[m,M]$ and $\varphi$ is continuous on $[m,M]$, then $\varphi\circ u$ is integrable ([[thm-composition-with-a-continuous-function]]); an integrable function is bounded, so such $m$ and $M$ exist ([[def-darboux-sums]], [[def-bounded-set]], [[def-interval]]).
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations.prompt.md-138-
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations.prompt.md:139:[L2] Sums and scalar multiples of integrable functions are integrable, with $\int_a^b(\lambda u + \nu w) = \lambda\int_a^b u + \nu\int_a^b w$ ([[thm-linearity-of-the-integral]]).
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations.prompt.md-140-
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations.prompt.md-141-[L3] If $u \le w$ pointwise on $[a,b]$ and both are integrable then $\int_a^b u \le \int_a^b w$ ([[thm-monotonicity-of-the-integral]]).
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-refuter-cor-integrability-of-absolute-values-products-and-lattice-operations.prompt.md-142-
