research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-12761-items/cex-absolute-value-integrable-without-the-function.md:73:1.1 $|f|$ is the constant function $1$ on $[0,1]$: at a rational $x$, $f(x) = 2\cdot1 - 1 = 1$, and at an irrational $x$, $f(x) = 2\cdot0-1 = -1$, and $|1| = |-1| = 1$ by [L1] and [L8]. Hence $|f|$ is integrable with $\int_0^1|f| = 1$ by [L7]. [given, L1, L7, L8]
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-12762-items/cex-absolute-value-integrable-without-the-function.md:81:4.1 Hence $L(f,P) = \sum_{i<n}(-1)\Delta_i = -1$ and $U(f,P) = \sum_{i<n}1\cdot\Delta_i = 1$, by [L4], [L6] and [L3]. [step 3.1, L3, L4, L6]
