research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-12764-items/thm-integration-by-parts.md:54:[L2] A function differentiable at every point of $[a,b]$ is continuous there ([[cor-differentiable-implies-continuous]], [[def-continuity-real]]).
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-12765-items/thm-integration-by-parts.md:62:[L6] If $H$ is differentiable at every point of $[a,b]$ with $H'$ integrable there, then $\int_a^b H' = H(b)-H(a)$ ([[thm-ftc-second-part]]).
research/audit/wave11-dispatch/audit-beta-a4.log-12766-items/thm-integration-by-parts.md:64:[L7] Oriented limits are not needed here, $a<b$ throughout ([[def-oriented-integral]]).
